# The yew tree PAX carries as /bin/yew (px58; tools/mkyew builds it).
#
# yew is the modal terminal editor in wolf: the maintainer's C yew
# (tenseleyFlow/sagitta) ported to wolf byte for byte (Track 12, ruling
# #89), the editor PAX will carry. px58 measures what it asks of Linux
# and what PAX answers (notes/px58-yew-on-pax.md, tests/mpx5-yew); no
# line of yew is changed here.
#
# yew trunk at the time of px58 (2026-10-21): 77c1083 (tl30's merge,
# after yw03's 9bd219c: M-YW3, modal editing; yw04's PR #19 open, not
# merged), pinned in its own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.33 / lupin
# 0.1.54 / wolf-std cceda63. tools/mkyew builds it with THAT toolchain
# (the archive by the digest yew names, the std tree at the commit it
# names), not with kernel/wolf.pin's, as tools/mkpelt builds pelt, and
# as yew's own `tools/build --static` builds the shape PAX runs.
#
# The static binary depends on the libc.a it links: built in kasumi's
# localhost/px13-ubuntu (image ad8964505189: Ubuntu 24.04.5, libc6-dev
# 2.39-0ubuntu8.9), its digest is in notes/px58-yew-on-pax.md §B.
YEW_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/yew
YEW_REV=0ccb2c67661a2dd789b5ce86180d592370a79c31

# px82: launch trunk, 1066 commits after the preceding pin.
# Codeload source archive sha256, read twice on hasu.
YEW_SOURCE_SHA256=d2ef6674865306bf5bc910b0541814210069c981a70bdbefdbf7a11e6f54ef15
